# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Cargo.lock IS committed here, overriding the global ignore rule.
#
# OutLayer compiles this example inside the enclave and attests the hash of the
# resulting wasm. An unpinned dependency graph means the same source can compile to a
# different binary, and a measurement nobody can reproduce is not much of a
# measurement. It also keeps the build pinned to something the worker's compiler image
# (Rust 1.85) can actually resolve.
!Cargo.lock

# WASI build outputs
*.wasm
*.wat

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Environment
.env
.env.local
